WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.654 --> 00:00:03.240
(upbeat music)

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.457
- Strongly agree.
- Strongly disagree.

00:00:04.457 --> 00:00:06.820
- Somewhat agree.
- Somewhat disagree.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:07.653
- I would agree.
- Disagree.

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:12.150
- I hate that every week, I
have to inject my hormones,

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.598
like I get so angry that
cis people get it for free.

00:00:15.598 --> 00:00:17.460
- I know!
- And it's just natural.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.407
- Like you've got in your body,
like I got it in a drawer.

00:00:20.407 --> 00:00:22.907
(light music)

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.160
- [Producer] I would date
a cisgender individual.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.140
Three, two, one.

00:00:36.275 --> 00:00:38.337
(tense music)

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:39.690
- I've dated cis people in the past

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:41.855
and every time, especially because I'm

00:00:41.855 --> 00:00:44.700
assigned female at birth and nonbinary,

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.470
if I'm dating a man, he typically
just sees me as a woman.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:51.240
I saw a TikTok literally yesterday,

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.190
it was like, "Have y'all ever
been with a they/them woman?"

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:56.610
I was like, that is so no.
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:59.310
- If you can't see me as nonbinary,

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:01.500
I cannot be seen outside with you.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:04.050
Like with women that are
cis, it's more welcoming,

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:06.510
but they perceive us as a lesbian couple

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:10.260
and that's not what really
what I'm trying to do.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:13.980
- At my age, boys kind
of come into themselves

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:16.740
and their desires and
it's just weird because

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:19.050
they either want one
thing or another thing

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.530
and usually I'm subject to be fetishized.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:25.117
Some guys will come at me and be like,

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:27.270
"Yeah, you're like the
best of both worlds,"

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:31.020
and I'm like, "Girl, this
is not 'Hannah Montana.'"

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.370
I am a girl.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:35.130
I want to have my own little moment where

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:36.960
I could just get my own Prince Charming

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.810
and stuff like that and just
have a normal relationship

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.850
like the rest of these cis girls.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:45.540
- For me, I normally have dated cis girls.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:48.540
I've been fetishized
probably a couple times,

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:49.980
like they say, "Oh, yeah, I'm bi,"

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:53.970
and they see me as a girl or something.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:55.410
It's so bizarre.

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:59.790
But I've only recently ever
dated someone who's not cis

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:02.430
and they identify as nonbinary and

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.530
that relationship taught me so much

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:08.010
because I feel like they
really saw me for who I am

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:11.310
and they were the most aware person.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.770
- I've only been with one cis person

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.480
and it was a girl and I feel like,

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.610
if anything, girls are
super understanding.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:21.000
But I'm still open to a cis person.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.470
It depends on the person, really,

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:24.390
like I'm not looking for a trans person,

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:26.790
I'm just looking for a good person.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:27.810
- [Producer] You should be able

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:30.810
to medically transition before adulthood.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:33.150
Three, two, one.

00:02:35.322 --> 00:02:37.500
(tense music)
- A lot of us,

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.730
we have realized that this
is what's best for us as kids

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:44.280
and it's all about your
mental health and wellbeing,

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.750
but, also, that being said,

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.550
I think it's also important that

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:48.990
this is what you really want

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:51.690
because it's going to be
a life-changing decision

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:54.090
and behind that, there should be a lot of

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:56.670
evaluations and a lot of affirmations.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.230
- That's basically what I was gonna say.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.370
- Yeah, me too.
- It's like,

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:00.840
it depends where you're at.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.310
You have to be at a certain place

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:04.260
and make sure you're really ready,

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:05.670
but I do think it would help

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:08.010
so many trans kids' mental health

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:10.950
if they were able to transition before 18.

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:13.740
- I'm dying to get on hormones and

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:17.670
I do agree that kids should be able to

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:20.550
get hormones and go through HRT,

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:23.580
but there's also a little
part of me that's like,

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:25.770
what if they end up changing their mind?

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:28.170
- Like when I was 13, I
thought I was a trans man

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:30.600
and then I was like, nah.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.250
And then I was like, wait.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.860
So for me, it was a lot of questioning

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:36.360
and going through different identities

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.100
until I found what felt right

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.002
and at the point I'm at right now,

00:03:40.002 --> 00:03:42.870
I don't even know if I want to go on HRT.

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:45.150
So if I would've went on
that when I was on 13,

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:47.160
I don't know, I don't think
I would've regretted it,

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.980
but I'm glad that I
internalized a lot of it

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.750
and went through it within myself.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.280
- I think so long as we educate children

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:56.130
on the risk on transitioning very young,

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:57.450
like medically transitioning very young

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.180
and they're educated on the process,

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:02.550
I think children should be able to choose

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:05.326
whether or not they want
to transition young.

00:04:05.326 --> 00:04:08.026
- [Producer] My teachers are
accepting of my pronouns.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:11.370
Three, two, one.

00:04:14.172 --> 00:04:17.160
(tense music)

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:20.040
- I went to UCI for a quarter and

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.300
they were very understanding and

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:22.740
they don't really ask questions,

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:25.080
but in high school, it
was definitely a struggle

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:27.840
because my name was a
different name on the roster

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.820
and then I would have to explain,

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:31.830
especially with my Spanish teacher,

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:33.930
she had such Catholic beliefs

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:36.630
and she would pull me
aside and ask questions

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:38.940
and it was really sweet of
her to try and understand,

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:42.150
but it was also hard for them to remember

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:45.180
in class and stuff like that,
so it was kind of a struggle.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.070
- I'm honestly really thankful that

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:50.640
they really did try to find a
way to make trans people feel

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.410
a bit more comfortable in the school.

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:55.320
Like right now, I'm taking
a ballet and Pilates class

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.337
and I totally thought it was gonna be,

00:04:57.337 --> 00:04:59.617
"Oh, but you're born male,

00:04:59.617 --> 00:05:03.120
"so you have to do
masculine-presenting stuff,"

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:04.830
which I was really afraid of,

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:08.580
but I'm so glad that
they're really accepting.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:09.960
- I go to UC Berkeley right now

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:12.810
and I get misgendered
there on a daily basis.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:14.910
I will introduce myself to the teacher

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.147
and I'll be like, "I go
by they/them pronouns,

00:05:16.147 --> 00:05:18.600
"by the way, I'm nonbinary,
please respect my pronouns,"

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:21.690
and within two times that
I'm in the classroom,

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:23.580
they'll go back to using she/her pronouns

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:26.130
and other classmates
will also misgender me

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:28.860
and it gets just really
mentally taxing at a point

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:31.614
and so I kind of just stop trying as much

00:05:31.614 --> 00:05:34.350
'cause it's just mentally exhausting

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:37.470
having to realize no one
sees you as nonbinary

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:40.890
because you still have feminine
qualities about yourself.

00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:43.680
- [Producer] I have
come out more than once.

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:45.690
Three, two, one.

00:05:48.259 --> 00:05:50.070
(tense music)

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:51.900
- I've come out multiple times.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:53.940
Not just for my trans experience,

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.640
but for my sexuality as well 'cause

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:59.970
I came out as pansexual,
then I came out as bi,

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:02.220
and then I just came out as nonbinary

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:05.100
before I came out as
trans, I'm like, oh my god,

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:06.960
when am I gonna get it right, y'all, like.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:08.490
- Yeah, same, I think I went through

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:10.080
four or five different sexualities

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:11.370
and then I was like wait (laughs).

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:13.320
And then I just feel like
presenting more androgynous,

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:15.090
it is this struggle of
coming out every day

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:17.497
and being like, "Hey,
I know I look this way,

00:06:17.497 --> 00:06:20.040
"but this is what I am,
this is how I feel."

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:22.293
And you can respect it
or not, like honestly.

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:26.430
I feel like it's just gonna be forever.

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:29.520
- I kind of feel like I have
to come out every single day

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:31.620
just like with the new
people I meet in my life,

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.697
I'm constantly having
to be like, "Oh, yeah,

00:06:33.697 --> 00:06:35.737
"my name's Mandy, I'm nonbinary,
I go by they/them pronouns,

00:06:35.737 --> 00:06:36.727
"please respect those pronouns

00:06:36.727 --> 00:06:38.640
"or this is not a safe space for me."

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:41.430
- I get telling people on a daily basis,

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:44.760
like anyone you meet, like I
want people to know immediately

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:46.860
that I'm trans 'cause I don't
want to bring it up later on

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:48.090
and have it be an issue with them.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.970
I feel like I only came out once

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:55.530
because after the first time,
I kind of made it visible

00:06:55.530 --> 00:06:57.390
and I didn't want to talk about it,

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.040
I didn't want to have to come out again

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:01.920
and I thankfully had very
supportive people in my life

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:05.340
that I could've came out to again,

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:07.230
but I felt a lot more comfortable

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:09.150
just kind of living my
life and having people

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:11.790
just accept what I'm doing with my life

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:14.103
without coming out again.

00:07:14.971 --> 00:07:16.740
- [Producer] Cisgender individuals

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:19.380
do not understand my struggles.

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:21.690
Three, two, one.

00:07:23.807 --> 00:07:26.340
(tense music)

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:29.610
- Personally, my friends try to empathize

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:31.740
and I really appreciate that for them.

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:34.740
But personally, I think that cis people

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:38.400
take for granted their gender euphoria.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:40.740
Getting ready in the morning
and looking at yourself

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:43.380
and having the absence of distress,

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.390
like when I get up and I get ready

00:07:45.390 --> 00:07:47.160
and I look at myself, physically,

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:49.380
I'm distressed, I don't
look like the person

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:52.050
I was just dreaming I was, you know?

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:54.750
- Like I've known people that were cis

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:57.240
and would kind of be
transphobic towards me

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:59.490
and after a few years,
they start transitioning

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:01.110
and they're like, "Oh, I understand now."

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:03.450
And it wasn't until they
were going through it

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:05.250
and really felt the pain of it

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:07.470
that they were able to understand.

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:10.200
- I try to think of just
the whole entire spectrum

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:14.730
of just cis people who
are identifying female,

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:18.120
but for some reason their
bodies present more masculine,

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:21.000
I feel like they can have
that sort of point of view

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:24.720
that can help them sympathize
and empathize for you more.

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:27.330
It's all about the spectrum and just how

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:29.133
there's just so many nuances.

00:08:30.202 --> 00:08:32.802
- [Producer] Life would be
easier if I wasn't trans.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:35.433
Three, two, one.

00:08:39.531 --> 00:08:42.960
(tense music)
- My whole thing is

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.390
I'm already a person of color.

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:46.920
If I wasn't nonbinary, I'd be a woman,

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:48.783
so life is not gonna be easy for me.

00:08:48.783 --> 00:08:51.030
I just feel like it wouldn't be the same,

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:53.040
but it wouldn't be necessarily easier.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:54.840
- I mean, I agree with
what you're saying about

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:57.690
being a person of color and being queer,

00:08:57.690 --> 00:09:00.930
but, you know, I've been through so much

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:03.420
horrible shit and, personally,

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:05.550
my life would be easier if I was cis.

00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:06.870
I mean, a defining part of

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:08.970
who I am is definitely being trans,

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:12.300
but every day, I do wonder
what if I was actually

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:15.300
born a cis female, you know?

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:18.360
- Yeah, I hate that I still
think a lot of the time,

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:22.020
like I wonder what life
would be like if I was cis

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.640
or I kinda wish I was cis.

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:25.197
Like I know I wouldn't be where I am

00:09:25.197 --> 00:09:27.600
and I wouldn't know
almost anyone in my life

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:30.120
if I wasn't trans and if I
didn't go through the struggles

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:31.050
I went through.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:34.140
I hate that every week I
have to inject my hormones,

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:37.595
like I get so angry that
cis people get it for free.

00:09:37.595 --> 00:09:39.210
- I know!
- It's just natural.

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:40.620
- Oh my god!
- Like wait.

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:43.830
- And there's times where my
insurance is being annoying

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:44.920
and I can't get my hormones.

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:45.840
- Yeah, you've got it in your body,

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:48.450
I got it in a drawer.
- Yeah.

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:51.870
It's really, really
hard and breaks me down,

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:56.220
but I know that I wouldn't be
who I am if I wasn't trans.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:57.480
- Yeah, just bouncing off that.

00:09:57.480 --> 00:10:00.626
Just the thought of waking
up and not having dysphoria

00:10:00.626 --> 00:10:03.690
about something and not
trying on 15 different shirts

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:05.130
because my chest doesn't look flat enough

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:06.660
or just stuff like that,

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:08.700
I think it would generally
make my life easier,

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:10.440
but again, it's like I
wouldn't meet the people

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:12.510
that I have in my life and
I'm so grateful for them.

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:13.933
- [Producer] And that will be it.

00:10:14.979 --> 00:10:16.692
So give yourselves a round of applause.

00:10:16.692 --> 00:10:21.692
(all clapping)
(gentle music)

00:10:40.377 --> 00:10:43.509
- I'm proud to be a citizen of my country.

00:10:43.509 --> 00:10:48.509
♪ Proud to be an American ♪
(all chuckling)

